});

if (require.main === module) {
  app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => {
    console.log(`Server running on http://${HOST}:${PORT}`);
  });
}

module.exports = app;
```

Notable extras in this refactor:
- `parseInt(..., 10)` guards against string-vs-number issues with env vars.
- `require.main === module` guard prevents the server from auto-starting when the module is imported by tests — useful since `module.exports = app` suggests test imports are expected.
- Interpolated log message stays correct when `PORT`/`HOST` change.

